**Description**
Removes the eval() of operation-output <script> blocks from OutputWaiter and adds script-src to the Docker image's CSP.

- Operations no longer emit <script>. Entropy, Frequency distribution, Index of Coincidence, Parse colour code, Show on map,
  Magic and Show Base64 offsets declare their widgets (bar/scale charts, colour picker, map, tooltips) with data-* attributes;
  src/web/utils/htmlOutputWidgets.mjs initialises them. Leaflet is loaded by the web layer, pinned with SRI.
  Show on map re-validates coordinates before emitting them. id="chart-area" is kept on chart canvases (Nightwatch relies on it).
- Docker: script-src 'self' 'unsafe-eval' blob: https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js (full path, not the host) + SHA-256 hashes of the app's own inline scripts
  (including the Bombe SVG's script and onload handler, hence 'unsafe-hashes'). No 'unsafe-inline'. Hashes are generated from the
  build output by scripts/generate-nginx-conf.mjs in the Dockerfile builder stage.
- The headers are shipped as /etc/nginx/conf.d/security-headers.conf instead of replacing the base image's default.conf. The
  replacement broke nginx startup on hosts without IPv6 (the base entrypoint only rewrites the packaged default.conf).
- object-src changes from 'none' to data: because 'none' stopped the Bombe loading animation (a data: URI <object>) from loading.
- 'unsafe-eval' stays: dependencies compile code at runtime (e.g. Handlebars in Template); it also covers WebAssembly.

